{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6841?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A6841"}, "created": "1978-07-01T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-10T10:04:14.311145+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "18", "artid": "3705", "year": 1978, "page_start": "3705", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Mueller, Alfred H."}], "texkeys": ["Mueller:1978xu"], "abstracts": [{"value": "Cut vertices, a generalization of matrix elements of composite operators, are introduced. Their renormalization is discussed. The Bogolubov-Parasiuk-Hepp-Zimmermann method of renormalization of cut vertices allows one to obtain a generalization of the Wilson expansion where cut vertices multiplied by singular functions appear rather than local operators times singular functions. A Callan-Symanzik equation for the moments of the structure function in e++e\u2212\u2192hadron\u00a0(p)+anything is derived. This equation is valid to all orders of perturbation theory in both gauge and nongauge theories. Examples of renormalization through the two-loop level are given."}], "control_number": 6841, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.18.3705"}], "titles": [{"title": "Cut Vertices and their Renormalization: A Generalization of the Wilson Expansion"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "6841"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C18%2C3705&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publi